<BaseLayout title="Fluids and capacities">
  <h1>Fluids and capacities</h1>
  <p>Use the fluid specification for the exact engine, transmission, and market. The values below are drawn from the 2021 S60 owner's information; confirm the under-hood label and VIN-specific service information before purchasing or filling fluids.</p>

  <h2>Engine oil — identify the engine first</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Required grade</th><td>Volvo specification VCC RBS0-2AE, SAE 0W-20</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Applicability</th><td>The figures below are the T5 AWD reference only. Do not assume they apply to T6, T8 Recharge, or every market/engine code.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Approximate volume including filter</th><td>5.6 L / 5.9 US qt</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Volvo says not to use oil additives. The volume is approximate: do not pour the full nominal capacity in blindly. Follow the correct service procedure and verify the electronic oil-level reading under the conditions specified in the owner's manual.</p>

  <p class="note"><strong>T5 / T6 / T8 note.</strong> Oil grade and capacity are engine-code-specific. T8 also has hybrid-system cooling circuits; do not treat those as part of the ordinary engine-coolant fill procedure. Use the VIN-specific Volvo specification for the exact engine and system being serviced.</p>

  <h2>Coolant</h2>
  <p>Use Volvo-approved premixed coolant. The owner's information says that if concentrate is used, it should be mixed 50/50 with water of suitable quality. Do not open a hot cooling system; it is pressurized and can cause serious burns.</p>

  <h2>Brake fluid</h2>
  <p>Volvo specifies original fluid or an equivalent meeting the combined DOT 4, DOT 5.1, and ISO 4925 Class 6 requirements. Volvo recommends that filling or replacement be performed by an authorized workshop.</p>

  <h2>Automatic transmission fluid</h2>
  <p>Volvo lists different fluids by gearbox: TG-81SC uses AW-1, while AWF8G45/AWF8G55 use AW-2. T5, T6, and T8 applications may not use the same gearbox variant. The transmission fitted to this particular car has not yet been confirmed. Identify the gearbox by VIN or transmission designation before purchasing fluid; never choose AW-1 or AW-2 from the T5/AWD badge alone. Fluid level and temperature procedures are transmission-specific.</p>

  <h2>Washer fluid</h2>
  <p>Use automotive windshield-washer fluid suitable for the expected outside temperature. In freezing weather, use a winter-rated product and avoid plain water.</p>

  <h2>Do not guess these values</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Coolant system total capacity and drain/refill quantity.</li>
    <li>Transmission service-fill quantity and temperature/check procedure.</li>
    <li>Brake hydraulic system total capacity.</li>
    <li>Refrigerant type and charge quantity.</li>
  </ul>

